# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...): only what's
# been looked at and isn't ViewTouch's.
#
# SQLite takes its own mutexes in different orders while one thread closes
# a connection (sqlite3_close: the pager and the shared cache); never two
# threads at once on one connection, so no deadlock.
deadlock:pthreadMutexEnter
#
# Qt's HTTP thread deletes a request's upload device while the main thread
# deletes the finished reply (QNetworkAccessManager inside, not our code).
race:QNonContiguousByteDeviceThreadForwardImpl
#
# Qt's TLS set-up takes QSslSocketPrivate's mutex and then the TLS backends'
# list mutex (QSslServer's constructor, the first time), and elsewhere the
# other way round; all inside Qt Network, once, on the main thread (6.12).
deadlock:QSslSocketPrivate::tlsBackendInUse
